# Trivy ignore list — accepted findings that won't be fixed.
#
# Add CVE IDs here only after consciously deciding to accept the risk. Each
# entry MUST include:
#   • CVE ID (one per line)
#   • // reason: brief why we're accepting
#   • // expires: YYYY-MM-DD when to re-review (max 6 months out)
#
# Example:
#   CVE-2024-12345  // reason: only triggered by user-controlled input we
#                   // sanitize at the API layer; upstream fix pending.
#                   // expires: 2026-08-01
#
# When an expiry passes, remove the line and let CI re-flag the CVE. If still
# unfixed, document why and renew. This is the policy that keeps the ignore
# list from becoming a dumping ground.
#
# Reference docs: https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/
